# Hardware Architecture

## Smart Mirror Thin Client

The mirror-side computer is responsible for lightweight, latency-sensitive functions.

Planned hardware:

```text
Lenovo ThinkPad T580 motherboard

CPU:
Intel Core i5-8250U
4 cores / 8 threads

RAM:
16 GB DDR4

Storage:
256 GB SSD

GPU:
Intel UHD 620 integrated graphics

Battery:
Removed

Power:
USB-C PD adapter
connected to PDU
```

The T580 BIOS supports:

```text
Power On with AC Attach
```

This should be enabled so the mirror automatically boots after power is restored.

The laptop's original LCD is not required. The motherboard will drive the smart mirror's large LCD using HDMI or USB-C/DisplayPort.

### Mirror Client Responsibilities

```text
Linux
│
├── Chromium kiosk
│   └── Eve dashboard
│
├── openWakeWord
│   └── "Hey Eve"
│
├── Silero VAD
│
├── microphone capture
│
├── speaker/audio playback
│
├── presence detection
│
├── display power control
│
├── WebSocket client
│
└── Eve edge service
```

The mirror client should remain mostly idle when Eve is not being used.

It should NOT perform the main LLM inference.

